  "design_notes": "Multinational, multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial conducted in 38 centres in Europe and the USA. Patients were randomised in a 2:1 ratio. Treatment duration was 48 weeks, with a 7-week follow-up. The primary endpoint was assessed by liver biopsy in the intention-to-treat population.",
  "population": {
    "condition": "non-alcoholic steatohepatitis (NASH)-related cirrhosis",
    "key_inclusion_criteria": [
      "male or female, aged 18–75 years (both inclusive) at the time of signing informed consent",
      "histological evidence of NASH and Kleiner F4 according to the NASH Clinical Research Network (CRN) classification",
      "liver biopsy obtained within 360 days before screening",
      "a histological non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) activity score (NAS) of 3 or more with a score of 1 or more for both lobular inflammation and hepatocyte ballooning",
      "body-mass index (BMI) of 27 kg/m2 or greater"
